TI  - LINEAR ENDOSONOGRAPHY IN LUNG CANCER: A COMPREHENSIVE REVIEW.
PG  - 35-43
LID - 10.48729/pjctvs.239 [doi]
AB  - The role of endobronchial ultrasound (EBUS) and trans-esophageal endobronchial 
      ultrasound (EUS-B) in lung cancer is well established and scientifically 
      validated. There is increasing data that endosonography is a crucial tool for the 
      diagnosis of central lung lesions, and mediastinal staging and restaging of 
      non-small cell lung cancer patients. The present article reviews the technical 
      aspects of EBUS and EUS-B and focus on the last published research regarding its 
      value in lung cancer.
