TI  - EUS-B FNA of Enlarged Left Adrenal Gland in Lung Cancer-Case Series.
PG  - e70618
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.70618 [doi]
LID - e70618
AB  - Combined endobronchial and endoscopic ultrasound via bronchoscope (EBUS EUS-B) is 
      an established method for diagnosis, staging and tissue acquisition in lung 
      cancer. With incorporation of EUS-B fine needle aspirate (EUS-B FNA) of enlarged 
      left adrenal gland (LAG), combined EBUS EUS-B can aid in excluding metastatic 
      spread or differentiating between regional (M1a) versus distant (M1b) single 
      organ or multi-organ metastatic disease (M1c). In comparing, EUS FNA of LAG via 
      conventional gastro-echoendoscope with EUS-B, conventional EUS can successfully 
      visualise LAG more frequently. However, once visualization is achieved, outcomes 
      in terms of diagnostic yield and tissue adequacy are comparable. Complication and 
      adverse event rates are low. EUS-B FNA of LAG is aligned with patient-centric 
      benefits of combined EBUS EUS-B. In our case series, we illustrate the use of 
      EUS-B FNA for diagnosis, staging and tissue acquisition in lung cancer. We 
      highlight learning points, discuss risk and benefits and advocate for broader 
      integration into clinical practice.
