TI  - Esophageal ultrasound with ultrasound bronchoscope (EUS-B) guided left adrenal 
      biopsy: Case report with review of literature.
PG  - 154-156
LID - 10.1016/j.rmcr.2018.12.012 [doi]
AB  - A 45-year old man, chronic smoker with a pancoast tumor due to squamous cell 
      carcinoma has been described. The initial diagnosis of lung carcinoma was based 
      on a scant tissue so the exact cell typing was not possible. The initial 
      treatment consisted of platinum based chemotherapy and radiotherapy. He developed 
      a left adrenal lesion on treatment. There was a possibility of metachronous 
      primary. Also, a large tissue sample was required for tumor markers. The lung 
      mass was difficult to access and was static on treatment. A left adrenal biopsy 
      was considered to be more appropriate. A novel approach for left adrenal lesion 
      with esophageal ultrasound using ultrasound bronchoscope (EUS-B) was successfully 
      performed. This article is aimed at describing the use of EUS-B for 
      transdiaphragmatic structures.
